  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive (fan / pump)",
  "applies_to": "Yaskawa P7 (CIMR-P7U) fan and pump drives using the built-in RS-422/485 terminals R+/R-/S+/S-, per user manual TM.P7.01 Appendix D.",
  "summary": "The P7 is Yaskawa's legacy variable-torque fan and pump drive with an embedded Modbus RTU slave (plus Metasys N2 and APOGEE FLN). Commands go to hex registers 0001H-000FH and status, fault, PI levels and diagnostics are read from 0020H-003FH. This map covers the full Appendix D reference and monitor data tables and the Enter commands.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 31,
    "baud": 9600,
    "parity": "None",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "hex 0-based",
    "note": "Register numbers are hex and are sent unchanged: the 03H example reads starting address 00 20 (drive status) and the 10H example writes 0001H (run forward) and 0002H (0258H = 600 for 60.0 Hz) starting at 00 01."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": null,
  "source": {
    "title": "P7 Drive User Manual (Appendix D Communications)",
    "doc_number": "TM.P7.01",
    "revision_date": null,
    "url": "https://www.yaskawa.com/delegate/getAttachment?documentId=TM.P7.01&cmd=documents&documentName=TM.P7.01.pdf",
    "pages": "Appendix D: specifications p. D-2, H5 table p. D-4, function examples pp. D-7 to D-8, data tables pp. D-9 to D-12"
  },
  "notes": [
    "TM.P7.01 does not print Modbus addresses for parameters (b1, H5) or for the U1/U2/U3 monitors, so only the Appendix D data-table registers are included; set b1/H5 at the keypad.",
    "0023H/0024H are listed raw: the units of U1-01/U1-02 change with o1-03 and no resolution is given in the data table.",
    "Left out because the manual prints no units or resolution: 0025H output voltage, 0026H output current, 0027H output power, 0028H torque reference and 0031H DC bus voltage.",
    "Broadcast (address 0) accepts only 0001H (bit 0 run, bit 1 reverse, bit 4 external error, bit 5 fault reset, bits C-E S5-S7) and 0002H (30000 = 100 %)."
  ],
